# What this build (game v1.4.0) changed that the framework cares about:
#   - New Graveyard buy-back system: State.GRAVEYARD (appended at the enum END,
#     so compiled mods keep working), GraveyardManager/Canvas/Button/Infos,
#     PieceManager.AddPieceToGraveyard, BaseData.Graveyard/GraveyardPieceBought.
#     The state machine can now pass WIN -> GRAVEYARD -> SHOP after boss levels.
#     KamikazeGambit feeds sacrificed pieces into the pool (via reflection, so
#     its prebuilt DLL still loads on pre-graveyard builds).
#   - WarHorse gambit replaced IN PLACE by Clown: Unlock_Infos.WAR_HORSE ->
#     CLOWN at the same ordinal (no enum shift), BaseData.WarHorse_Unlock ->
#     Clown_Unlock, types Gambit_WarHorse/WarHorse_GambitUnlock removed,
#     Gambit_Clown/Clown_GambitUnlock added. Vanilla gambit count is still 200.
#   - GambitLibrary.SelectGambits now dedups on SO_Gambit.GambitName instead of
#     UnityEngine.Object.name (GambitApi already assigns both uniquely).
#   - SettingsCanvas gained a sixth "Accessibility" tab (m_Accessibility /
#     m_AccessibilityContainer) plus ~5 new gameplay-tab rows (Skip Animations,
#     Ask Before Open Graveyard, Cursor, Shake Screen, Tile Coordinates).
#     Tab BUTTONS are discovered by field TYPE (ButtonSettings) since framework
#     v1.1.0 - the old name-suffix match missed m_Customize/m_Accessibility and
#     they leaked into cloned mod modals.
#   - New types the framework doesn't bind: BoardStructureManager, SkipBossUI,
#     AchievementType, RunInfo_AchievementHint, AccessibiltySettings (sic),
#     WarningSettingsBehaviour, GraveyardButton.
#   - Audited ~112 reflection/compile-time bindings across 36 game types:
#     everything else the framework touches (GameManager.Start,
#     CanvasMenu.OnEnable, SettingsCanvas.OnEnable, GambitLibrary buckets,
#     GambitCollectionSlide, RunInfoCanvas, StockManager, ChessDataManager,
#     TileBehaviour, BossManager, LocalizationManager, scheme/customize types)
#     is unchanged. Assets grew to 925 sprites / 236 textures (gallery: 561/236).
